======================================================================
(C) LAW CHECK on primitive 5-sets: debt-zero <=> 0 not sign-reachable mod3 <=> k<=1
======================================================================
  tested 201 primitive 5-sets; law (no-debt <=> 0-not-reachable-mod3 <=> k<=1) holds: 200/201
  debt-FREE sets found: []
  (debt-free require exactly one runner != 0 mod 3, the rest divisible by 3)

======================================================================
(D) n=4 parallel: units mod 2 = {1} -> single sum 'a+b+c odd' (no sign freedom)
======================================================================
   (a,b,c) : sum  parity   debt-free(no odd-coeff resonance)?
   (1, 2, 3) :  6  even   debt-free=False  (predict False)
   (1, 2, 4) :  7  odd    debt-free=True  (predict True)
   (1, 3, 5) :  9  odd    debt-free=True  (predict True)
   (2, 3, 4) :  9  odd    debt-free=True  (predict True)
   (1, 1, 1) :  3  odd    debt-free=True  (predict True)
   (1, 2, 5) :  8  even   debt-free=False  (predict False)
   => n=4: ONE fixed sum mod 2 (units {1}). n=6: SIGNED sum mod 3 (units {+-1})
      = the first genuinely multi-channel parity law; mod6 = mod3 (x) mod2-sign.
